🛸 UFO Sighting Data Preprocessing & Machine Learning Pipeline
An end-to-end machine learning and data preprocessing portfolio project built using Python, Pandas, NumPy, and Scikit-Learn. This project demonstrates advanced data cleaning, feature engineering, text vectorization via TF-IDF, and supervised classification modeling on real-world sighting records.

🛠️ Complete Project Workflow & Technical Highlights
1. Data Cleaning & Missing Value Treatment
Inspected dataset columns for missing or null values across critical features.

Dropped incomplete records in key subsets (length_of_time, state, type) to ensure robust model training data.

2. Regular Expressions & Feature Extraction
Parsed messy, unstructured duration strings into clean numeric columns (minutes) utilizing Python's re module.

Extracted temporal attributes (month, year) from timestamp data using Pandas datetime accessors (.dt).

3. Log Normalization & Variance Reduction
Analyzed feature distributions and identified extreme variance in the seconds duration column.

Applied natural log transformations (np.log) to compress the scale and generate seconds_log, stabilizing feature variance for modeling.

4. Categorical & Binary Encoding
Performed binary mapping via conditional lambda functions to encode target location labels (us vs. ca).

Implemented one-hot encoding (pd.get_dummies) on categorical sighting descriptors (type) and merged the resulting dummy matrices back into the primary DataFrame.

5. Natural Language Processing (NLP) & TF-IDF Vectorization
Transformed unstructured narrative description fields (desc) into dense numerical feature matrices using TF-IDF Vectorization (TfidfVectorizer).

Filtered text vocabulary using custom functions to isolate high-signal predictive tokens.

6. Supervised Machine Learning Models
K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN): Trained on engineered numerical, temporal, and one-hot encoded features with stratified train-test splits (stratify=y, random_state=42) to predict sighting locations.

Multinomial Naive Bayes (NB): Trained on high-dimensional sparse TF-IDF text vectors to successfully classify sighting characteristics and types based on textual descriptions.

